# Kings Equestrian Operations — Web App Guide

Spreadsheet: **Kings Equestrian Operations Master.xlsx** (Google Sheets when deployed).  
Code: `code.js` + HTML forms. Deploy via Google Apps Script (copy files, new deployment, hard refresh).

Also see: `SHEETS_SETUP.md` for sheet column quick reference.

---

## 1. Spreadsheet tabs (data model)

| Tab | Role |
|-----|------|
| **Users** | Login: Email, Password, Role (`Admin` / `Trainer` / `Groom`), **Name** (must match Trainers/Grooms name for routine filtering), Location |
| **Locations** | Location_ID, Location_Name (e.g. Farm, LOC004) |
| **Horses** | Horse_ID, Horse_Name, Breed, Age, Location, Owner, Status, Gender |
| **HorseProfile** | Trainer, Groom, Weight, Facility Multiplier, Lease, Present medication, standard feed/water (pre-fill Daily Routine) |
| **Trainers** | Trainer_Name, Specialization, Location, Phone, Experience_Years, Status |
| **Grooms** | Groom_Name, Location, Phone, Shift, Status |
| **Raw Data** | Every stock movement: Date, Location, Item, Entry Type (`Opening` / `Added` / `Consumption`), Quantity |
| **Daily Inventory** | Aggregated per location+item+date: Opening, Added, Consumption, **Closing** |
| **Inventory Items** | Item list + optional min/reorder levels |
| **DailyRoutineLog** | One row per horse per save: activities, feed slots, water, totals |
| **inventory_transaction** | Audit: Timestamp, Location, Item, Quantity, Type, Reference |
| **HorseHealthData** | Daily health checks |
| **MedicalHistory** | Medical incidents / treatments |
| **VaccinationData** | Vaccines, dates, next due |
| **ShoeingData** | Farrier visits, next shoeing due |
| **ActivityData** | Legacy activity log (optional) |

**Auto-created on first routine save:** HorseProfile, DailyRoutineLog, inventory_transaction (if missing).

---

## 2. Deploy & login

1. Apps Script project bound to the master spreadsheet.  
2. Add all `form-*.html`, `Dashboard.html`, `AppChrome.html`, `code.js`.  
   - **AppLoader** is inlined in **`AppChrome.html`** (no separate file).  
   - **AppViewport** (`google.script.host.setWidth` / `setHeight`) is **inlined in `AppChrome.html`**; login page has the same script inlined.  
3. Deploy → Web app → execute as you, access by link.  
4. Open the **deployed web app URL** (`script.google.com/macros/s/.../exec`), not only the Apps Script editor preview iframe (preview often adds side margins).  
5. Login with **Users** sheet credentials.  
6. **Admin:** can switch location in header; default view often Farm (LOC004).  
7. **Trainer / Groom:** fixed location; Daily Routine shows only horses where **HorseProfile.Trainer** or **HorseProfile.Groom** = **Users.Name**.

### Mobile / iframe full width

The app sets `html.app-fullwidth` when loaded inside Google’s iframe, on `script.google.com` / `googleusercontent.com`, or on screens under 1200px wide. That removes the old `max-width: 720px` centering that caused empty space on the left and right. On large desktop browsers only (≥1200px, top-level window), content may center in a 1100px column for readability.

On screens **768px and below**, the four dashboard summary cards stack **one per row** (full width), with larger text (labels ~13px, main numbers ~36px, card lines ~15px) for easier reading on phones.

**GAS iframe scaling:** **`AppChrome.html`** (and **`code.js`** `addMetaTag` viewport) does three things on phones:
1. `google.script.host.setWidth(realPhoneWidth)` — uses `visualViewport` / short side of `screen`, not the ~760px iframe `innerWidth`.
2. **CSS `zoom` fallback** — if the iframe stays wide, scales the page to fit (~360px) so text is readable.
3. `setHeight(content height)` — iframe height matches content (removes large empty gap at the bottom).  
Also sets `html.app-mobile` with **18px** base font and larger dashboard card text. Redeploy **`code.js`**, **`AppChrome.html`**, and **`Dashboard.html`**.

---

## 3. Dashboard — each widget

Backend entry: `getDashboardData(token, viewLocation)` → `buildDashboardPayload_()` → `filterDashboardPayload_(location)`.

### 3.1 Location bar (Admin)

- **Shows:** Chips for All + each location from **Locations**.  
- **Data:** `getLocationsList_()`.  
- **Effect:** Re-fetches dashboard with `viewLocation`; all counts/lists filter to that site.

### 3.2 Dashboard — four summary boxes (2×2 grid)

The home dashboard shows **four stat-style square cards** (same visual style as the horse count card). All values respect the selected **location** filter.

#### Box 1 — Horses

| Display | Source | Calculation |
|---------|--------|-------------|
| **Large number** — total horses | **Horses** | Count at this location |
| **Small text** — `Healthy: X · Rehab: Y` | **HorseHealthData** + horse status | Healthy = `🟢 Healthy`; Rehab = rehabilitation status on horse/profile |

**Example:** `3` with subtext `Healthy: 2 · Rehab: 1`

#### Box 2 — Staff

| Line | Source |
|------|--------|
| `Trainers: Active N · Leave M` | **Trainers** (`getStaffStatusCounts_`) |
| `Grooms: Active N · Leave M` | **Grooms** |
| `Name: K horses` (per trainer) | **HorseProfile** → Trainer column |
| `Name: K horses` (per groom) | **HorseProfile** → Groom column |

**Example:**

```
Trainers: Active 2 · Leave 1
Grooms: Active 3 · Leave 0
Raj: 2 horses
Priya: 1 horses
```

#### Box 3 — Stock Alerts

| Line | Source | Formula / logic |
|------|--------|-----------------|
| Feed (Mixed): *N days stock* | **Daily Inventory** | `floor(Closing ÷ Consumption)` for item name matching Feed (Mixed) |
| Barley: *N days stock* | Same | Match `Barley` |
| Dry grass: *N days stock* | Same | Match `Dry Grass` |
| Shoeing: Due in *N days* | **ShoeingData** | Nearest upcoming shoeing for horses at this location |

Shows `—` when no row or zero consumption. Item names in Raw Data / routine must match: `Feed (Mixed)`, `Barley`, `Dry Grass`, etc.

**Example:**

```
Feed (Mixed): 20 days stock
Barley: 15 days stock
Dry grass: 65 days stock
Shoeing: Due in 7 days
```

#### Box 4 — Health

| Line | Source | Logic |
|------|--------|--------|
| Vet check: Due in *N days* | **VaccinationData** | Nearest upcoming vaccine for location horses |
| De-worming: Due in *N days* | **VaccinationData** | Nearest row where vaccine matches /deworm/i |

**Example:**

```
Vet check: Due in 15 days
De-worming: Due in 60 days
```

If schedule data uses horse names not at this location (e.g. Zara on sheet but only Umber at Farm), lines show `—` until names align.

### 3.3 Alerts

Merged list (max ~5+5+3):

- **Shoeing** overdue / due soon (`getShoeingStatus`, alert ≠ OK)  
- **Vaccination** overdue / due soon (`getVaccinationStatus`)  
- **Stock** High consumption / Check status on **Daily Inventory** rows  

### 3.4 Horses tab (list)

- **Source:** `getHorsesList_` from **Horses** + health badge from latest **HorseHealthData**.  
- Filtered by selected location.

### 3.5 Staff tab (lists)

- **Trainers** / **Grooms** from respective sheets, location-filtered.  
- Buttons: **+ Add New Trainer**, **+ Add New Groom** → master forms.

### 3.6 Quick Entry & Forms tab

Links open forms via `buildAppPageUrl` (see Section 4).

---

## 4. Forms — files, fields, and what gets written

All submits go through `submitFormData(formKey, payload, token)` in `code.js`. Location is enforced from the user session unless Admin picks another allowed site.

| Form key | HTML file | On submit — sheets & rows |
|----------|-----------|---------------------------|
| **routine** / **activity** | `form-daily-routine.html` | **DailyRoutineLog** (1 row per horse with data); **Raw Data** (Entry Type `Consumption` per feed item total); **inventory_transaction** (`CONSUMPTION`); **Daily Inventory** updated incrementally via `updateDailyInventoryForConsumption_` (does **not** run full `generateInventory` on dashboard load) |
| **stock** | `form-daily-stock-entry.html` | **Raw Data** (Opening / Added / adjustment per headers); optional incremental **Daily Inventory** for that item+location+date |
| **health** | `form-health-medical.html` (health tab) | **HorseHealthData** — append row matching sheet headers |
| **medical** | `form-health-medical.html` (medical tab) | **MedicalHistory** — append row |
| **vaccination** | `form-vaccination.html` | **VaccinationData** — append row |
| **shoeing** | `form-shoeing-record.html` | **ShoeingData** — append row |
| **horse** | `form-add-horse.html` | **Horses** (new Horse_ID auto P001-style); **HorseProfile** (trainer, groom, defaults) |
| **trainer** | `form-add-trainer.html` | **Trainers** — rejects duplicate Trainer_Name |
| **groom** | `form-add-groom.html` | **Grooms** — Groom_Name, Location, Phone, Shift, Status; rejects duplicate name |

**Not wired to submitFormData:** `form-health-check.html`, `form-horse-activity.html`, `form-medical-record.html` (use Dashboard links to the wired forms instead).

### 4.1 Daily Routine (main operations form) — detail

**Loads from:** HorseProfile + Horses for location; 7AM feed pre-fill uses **Standard × Facility Multiplier × Weight ÷ 100** (kg); water defaults in **liters (L)**.

**Activity dropdowns:** Flatwork, Pole work, Lunging, Dressage, Jumping (+ Training, Exercise, Rest, Grooming, Turnout).

**Columns:** Horse name, **Present medication** (editable; syncs to HorseProfile on save), Activity 1/2, feed **(kg)** per slot, water **(L)**.

**Saves per horse row:**

1. **DailyRoutineLog** — Date, Location, Horse_ID, Horse_Name, Activity1/2, feed columns (7AM, 1PM, 6PM, Extra) for Wet Grass, Dry Grass, Feed (Mixed), Barley, Oats, water slots, totals, Present_Medication, Trainer, Groom, Logged_By.  
2. Sums feed totals across all horses → **consumption** map.  
3. **Raw Data** — one row per item: `{ Date, Location, Item, Entry Type: Consumption, Quantity }`.  
4. **inventory_transaction** — audit line per item.  
5. **Daily Inventory** — bumps Consumption and recalculates Closing for that date/location/item.

**Example consumption after one day at Farm (2 horses, 1 kg Barley each):**

```
Raw Data: 2026-05-21 | Farm | Barley | Consumption | 2
Daily Inventory: Farm | Barley | Consumption += 2 | Closing = Opening + Added - Consumption
```

**Access:** Trainers/grooms only see/edit horses assigned to them in HorseProfile.

### 4.2 Daily Stock Entry

**Purpose:** Record deliveries, opening stock, or manual adjustments.

**Writes:** **Raw Data** only (headers must include Date, Location, Item, Entry Type, Quantity).

**Example:**

```
2026-05-20 | Farm | Dry Grass | Opening | 100
2026-05-21 | Farm | Barley | Added | 50
```

Run `generateInventory()` manually or via daily 9 AM trigger to rebuild **Daily Inventory** from all Raw Data if numbers look wrong.

### 4.3 Add Horse / Edit Horse

**Fields:** Name, Breed, Age, Location, Owner, Gender, Status, Trainer, Groom, **Weight (kg)**, **Facility Multiplier**, **Lease** (rider name + date), **Present medication**, standard feed/water defaults (kg / L).

**Edit:** Dashboard → **Horses** tab → **Edit** on a horse card opens `form-add-horse` with `?horseId=…` (update mode).

**Feed default formula (Daily Routine 7AM pre-fill):**  
`Final feed (kg) = Standard Qty × Facility Multiplier × Horse Weight ÷ 100`

**Writes:**

- **Horses:** Horse_Name, Horse_ID (generated), Location, Weight, Lease, …  
- **HorseProfile:** assignments, weight, multiplier, medication, standard defaults for routine pre-fill.

**Daily Routine** also logs **Present_Medication** per entry and syncs it back to **HorseProfile** when saved.

### 4.4 Add Trainer / Add Groom

**Trainer → Trainers:** Trainer_Name, Specialization, Location, Phone, Experience_Years.

**Groom → Grooms:** Groom_Name, Location, Phone, Shift (Morning/Evening/Full Day), Status (Active/Leave/Inactive).

**Dashboard:** Forms → Master Data → Add New Groom (or Staff tab → + Add New Groom).

---

## 5. Inventory pipeline (how numbers flow)

```
Opening / Added  ──►  Raw Data  ──►  generateInventory() or incremental update
                              ──►  Daily Inventory (Opening, Added, Consumption, Closing)

Daily Routine save  ──►  Raw Data (Consumption)  ──►  updateDailyInventoryForConsumption_()
```

**Closing formula (per location + item + date):**  
`Closing = Opening + Added - Consumption` (aggregated in `scanRawInventoryAggregates_` / incremental updater).

**Stock days widget:** `floor(Closing / Consumption)` using the latest Daily Inventory row per item+location.

---

## 6. Roles & troubleshooting

| Issue | Cause | Fix |
|-------|--------|-----|
| Dashboard all zeros / timeout | Full sheet scans | Deploy latest `code.js` (bounded reads, no `generateInventory` on dashboard load) |
| Farm stock "0 items" | Wrong column names or row cap | Ensure Daily Inventory has Item, Location, Closing, Consumption; redeploy |
| Health Schedule empty at Farm | Vaccination/Shoeing horse names ≠ Horses at Farm | Add rows for `Umber` or move horse data to match |
| Trainer sees no horses | Users.Name ≠ HorseProfile.Trainer | Align spelling in **Users** and **HorseProfile** |
| Consumption not reducing stock | Item label mismatch | Use exact labels: Wet Grass, Dry Grass, Feed (Mixed), Barley, Oats |

**Users.Name** must match **Trainers.Trainer_Name** or **Grooms.Groom_Name** for assignment filtering.

---

## 7. Example data snapshot (reference)

From master workbook samples (your live sheet may differ):

- **Farm horse:** P005 Umber  
- **Shoeing/Vaccination samples:** often Zara, Sultan, Raja — link to correct location or horse name for widgets to show at Farm  
- **Admin user:** role Admin, can pick location in header  

---

## 8. Maintenance triggers

`setupTriggers()` in `code.js`:

- **9 AM daily:** `generateInventory()` — full rebuild Daily Inventory from Raw Data  
- **8 PM daily:** `dailyEmailReport()`  

Use **Deploy → Test deployments → Hard refresh** after code changes.

